      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this TODO brings much. The one condition is : this should be done before the first rematch or capabilities change after the network is connected, to avoid having caps updated callbacks for this immediately. It\u0027s fine to do it here, like it would be fine to do it in l.9188. I don\u0027t think there is any drawback to leaving it here, so I don\u0027t see the point of this TODO.\n\nThe one thing that can be said is, if we had updateCapabilities return after it\u0027s mixed in the capabilities (l.7956 in this patchset) if !everConnected, then we should be able to remove this line, and remove the test in l.9175, and always call updateCapabilitiesForNetwork in l.9179. It would clarify (and prove) that updateCapabilities never sends callbacks when the network is not everConnected, and would simplify usage of it because it would no longer be implicit in the code (e.g. here without this change you\u0027d have a capabilities callback in l.9179 if you only remove this line).\n\nNo strong opinion. If you choose to do the cleanup that I\u0027m suggesting it should be in another patch, and the TODO here should reflect that work. Otherwise, I think we can just remove this TODO.",
